    <rdfs:label>Late Effects: Heart Problems</rdfs:label>
    <dcterms:description>Explains potential heart problems following cancer treatment in young people, including relevant treatment exposures, symptoms to report, follow-up tests and measures to support heart health.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:identifier>MAYA-EDU-0018</dcterms:identifier>
    <dcterms:language rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#language">en</dcterms:language>
    <dcterms:publisher>Children's Cancer and Leukaemia Group (CCLG)</dcterms:publisher>
    <dcterms:rights>Link / Signpost Only</dcterms:rights>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="https://www.cclg.org.uk/about-cancer/living-beyond-cancer/late-effect-factsheets/heart-problems"/>
    <dcterms:title>Late Effects: Heart Problems</dcterms:title>
    <edu:accessConditions>Public</edu:accessConditions>
    <edu:applicabilityNotes>Particularly relevant to survivors treated as children, teenagers or young adults. Primarily concerns late effects and follow-up. Treatment-specific monitoring and exercise advice require individual clinical interpretation.</edu:applicabilityNotes>
